The attached image illustrates the uptake of AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) and FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA, green) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs), with nuclei stained by DAPI (blue) and actin by phalloidin (gray), using confocal microscopy. While soluble OVA alone showed minimal uptake by BMDCs, Nano-11 particles were efficiently phagocytized. When OVA was adsorbed to Nano-11 (OVA+Nano-11 complexes), the amount of intracellular OVA in BMDCs significantly increased, and both OVA and Nano-11 co-localized within the cells, indicating enhanced antigen delivery to dendritic cells.